&gt;the repository&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>SAT-SMT-AR summer school</title><link>https://ervinuelas.github.io/p/sat-smt-ar/</link><pubDate>Tue, 23 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ervinuelas.github.io/p/sat-smt-ar/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://ervinuelas.github.io/p/sat-smt-ar/sat-smt-ar.jpeg" alt="Featured image of post SAT-SMT-AR summer school" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;This summer I attended the &lt;a class="link" href="https://sat-smt-ar-school.gitlab.io/www/2024/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;SAT/SMT/AR summer school&lt;/a&gt; in Nancy, France. It was a very intense experience, I had the opportunity to learn about some of the ongoing research and the latest challenges in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Although all the lectures were very interesting, I have to admit that the ones given by &lt;a class="link" href="https://hanielbarbosa.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Haniel Barbosa&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.lri.fr/~keller/index-en.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Chantal Keller&lt;/a&gt; were the ones I enjoyed the most, since those were the ones that were more related to my bachelor thesis. Besides, I had the opportunity to meet a lot of colleagues who were doing research on the topics of the school, which was a very enriching experience from a professional and personal way.&lt;/p&gt;
